# Article: Pack (directed-cg, Director + Builder + Reviewer)

Roles launched by SwarmForge: builder, reviewer. The Director is the user's
normal Codex session and is not a third Herdr worker.

State machine: BUILD -> REVIEW -> ACCEPT, or one REPAIR -> DELTA REVIEW ->
ACCEPT/BLOCKED.

- The Director is the only coordinator. Workers receive direct prompts from
  the Director and report only to the Director.
- builder implements the bounded assignment in its isolated worktree, runs
  relevant verification, commits the result, and reports its SHA and evidence.
- reviewer inspects the exact candidate and base named by the Director. It is
  read-only: it does not edit tracked files or create commits. It reports one
  GO or NO-GO verdict with concrete evidence.
- One NO-GO may produce one bounded repair assignment. The reviewer then checks
  only the repair delta plus regressions relevant to it. A second NO-GO is
  terminal BLOCKED and goes to the user.
- Workers do not use handoff queues, message one another, launch subagents,
  broaden scope, merge into a protected branch, or push.
- Acceptance is a Director decision based on the stated acceptance criteria
  and verification evidence. Integration and push remain explicit user actions.
